# Keeps the Docker build context (all of it uploaded to the daemon, not just what a
# Dockerfile COPYs) small and -- more importantly -- keeps real secrets out of it
# entirely. deploy/relay/Dockerfile's builder stage does `COPY . .` because swarm-relay's
# module needs the whole tree to build; without this file that COPY would also land
# secrets/ (a real, gitignored credential -- see secrets/.gitignore) inside a cached
# image layer on whatever machine runs the build, which `docker history`/`docker save`
# would then expose regardless of what the final stage actually copies out of the builder.

secrets/
.git/
.claude/worktrees/
android/
dist/
*.db
*.test
# Operator-created local files the compose header instructs; never build-context material.
deploy/relay/relay.config
deploy/relay/Caddyfile.local
